sequenceDiagram
    title BLE Peripheral Complete Flow: Advertise, Connect, Pair, Bond

    participant App as App
    participant Node as Node<br>[implements GapPeripheral]
    participant Central as BLE Central

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over App, Central: 1. Configuration (optional)
        opt App overrides the default security profile
            App->>Node: GapPeripheral.SetSecurityPreferences(<br>secureConnections=enforced, mitm=enforced,<br>ioCapabilities=displayYesNo)
        end
        opt App overrides the default advertisement payload
            App->>Node: GapPeripheral.SetAdvertisementData(<br>data=0x0A 0x09 'N''o''n''i''n''3''1''5''0' 0x03 0x03 0x22 0x18)
            App->>Node: GapPeripheral.SetScanResponseData(<br>data=0x03 0x03 0x22 0x18)
        end
        Note over App: If skipped, defaults apply. Without SetAdvertisementData the Node<br>advertises only the flags AD field (no device name, no service UUIDs).<br>Pairing is allowed by default, so SetAllowPairing(true) is not needed.
    end

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over App, Central: 2. Start advertising
        App->>Node: GapPeripheral.Advertise(type=advInd, advertisingInterval=160)
        Note right of App: advertisingInterval=160 -> 100 ms<br>(units of 0.625 ms)
        Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.CurrentState(advertising)

        Note over App, Central: Node is now visible to BLE centrals
    end

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over App, Central: 3. Central connects
        Central->>Node: BLE connection request
        Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.CurrentState(connected)
    end

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over App, Central: 4. Pairing (initiated by central)
        Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.AuthenticationRequired(<br>isNumericComparison=true, passkey=485923)

        Note over App: User confirms numeric comparison on peripheral side

        App->>Node: GapPeripheral.NumericComparisonConfirm(true)
        Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.NumberOfBondsChanged(1)
        Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.PairingResult(pairedSuccessfully=true)

        Note over App: Bond stored. Peripheral is now bonded with the central.
    end

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over App, Central: 5. Disconnection
        Central--xNode: Peer disconnects
        Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.CurrentState(standby)

        Note over App: Can re-advertise to accept new connections.
    end
